{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3hPZAw2kRCivbLMch7ZQ4","type":"tool_result","content":"### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### interface SettingsHost\n\n2727:### class Particles\n2728-\n2729-Pixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\n2730-palette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\n2731-preset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\n2732-Available as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n2733-(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n2734-\n2735-  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n2736-  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n2737-\n2738-- `new Particles(view: () => ParticleView)`\n2739-- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`: Engine-owned group holding every emitter.\n2740-- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\n2741-- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83ee8bb7-9f1f-4db7-994e-0a6a2ece78a9","uuid":"333bc47e-1124-4d75-93a0-367c9b9bfd7e","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:30:08.620Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### class Settings\n\n`engine.settings`: the player's settings, applied to the engine and saved. A field the page URL\nsets (`?look=`, `?mode=`, `?res=`, `?quality=`, `?fps=`, `?debug=`: review flags) wins over a\nsaved one at start (which stays saved). `open`, `close` and `toggle` show and hide the\nsettings panel.\n\n- `new Settings(host: SettingsHost, key: string | null)`\n- `readonly key: string | null`\n- `get values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>`: The player's choices in effect: fields left out are the game's (or a review flag's).\n- `get isOpen: boolean`\n- `set(patch: PlayerSettings): void`: Change some settings: applied at once and saved. A field set to `undefined` goes back to the game's.\n- `reset(): void`: Forget every choice, the held ones too: the game's own picture again.\n- `replace(values: PlayerSettings): void`: Make `values` the settings, changing only the fields that differ: the ones it leaves out go back to the game's.\n- `onChange(fn: (values: Readonly<PlayerSettings>) => void): () => void`: Called with the values after every change; returns the unsubscribe.\n- `open(): void`\n- `close(): void`\n- `toggle(): void`\n\n### interface SettingsHost\n\n2727:### class Particles\n2728-\n2729-Pixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\n2730-palette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\n2731-preset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\n2732-Available as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n2733-(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n2734-\n2735-  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n2736-  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n2737-\n2738-- `new Particles(view: () => ParticleView)`\n2739-- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`: Engine-owned group holding every emitter.\n2740-- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\n2741-- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01B3hPZAw2kRCivbLMch7ZQ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
