{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0126VDctUAESqWUvrh2wWmDL","type":"tool_result","content":"### interface MergeOptions\n\n- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n\n### mergeStaticMeshes()\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n```\n\nMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\nmaterials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\ngroups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n\nWorld transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\ngroups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\nsources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\none collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\non screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves…\n\n### PALETTE\n\n3967:### class Boids\n3968-\n3969-- `new Boids(count: number, o: BoidOptions = {})`\n3970-- `readonly count: number`\n3971-- `readonly pos: Float32Array`\n3972-- `readonly vel: Float32Array`\n3973-- `o: Required<Omit<BoidOptions, 'bounds' | 'seed'>> & { bounds: BoidOptions['bounds'] }`\n3974-- `seek: Vec3 | null`: A point everyone is drawn toward (null: none).\n3975-- `seekWeight: number`\n3976-- `flee: { at: Vec3; radius: number } | null`: A threat to scatter from.\n3977-- `fleeWeight: number`\n3978-- `obstacles: { x: number; y: number; z: number; r: number }[]`: Spheres to steer around (x, y, z, r).\n3979-- `spacing(): number`: Average distance to the nearest neighbour (tests, tools).\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4591-\n4592-### type PrecipitationKind\n4593-\n4594-```ts","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83ee8bb7-9f1f-4db7-994e-0a6a2ece78a9","uuid":"60fe4eed-c3ab-433f-9e36-c98678c0dd24","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:30:25.770Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### interface MergeOptions\n\n- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n\n### mergeStaticMeshes()\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n```\n\nMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\nmaterials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\ngroups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n\nWorld transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\ngroups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\nsources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\none collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\non screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves…\n\n### PALETTE\n\n3967:### class Boids\n3968-\n3969-- `new Boids(count: number, o: BoidOptions = {})`\n3970-- `readonly count: number`\n3971-- `readonly pos: Float32Array`\n3972-- `readonly vel: Float32Array`\n3973-- `o: Required<Omit<BoidOptions, 'bounds' | 'seed'>> & { bounds: BoidOptions['bounds'] }`\n3974-- `seek: Vec3 | null`: A point everyone is drawn toward (null: none).\n3975-- `seekWeight: number`\n3976-- `flee: { at: Vec3; radius: number } | null`: A threat to scatter from.\n3977-- `fleeWeight: number`\n3978-- `obstacles: { x: number; y: number; z: number; r: number }[]`: Spheres to steer around (x, y, z, r).\n3979-- `spacing(): number`: Average distance to the nearest neighbour (tests, tools).\n4580:### class Precipitation\n4581-\n4582-- `new Precipitation(o: PrecipitationOptions)`\n4583-- `readonly kind: PrecipitationKind`\n4584-- `readonly area: readonly [number, number, number]`\n4585-- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind (m/s along x and z): rain slants, snow drifts.\n4586-- `get intensity: number`: Share of the drops falling (0..1).\n4587-- `get speed: number`: Fall speed (m/s).\n4588-- `update(dt: number, center: Vector3): void`: Per frame (game time): advance the fall and follow `center`.\n4589-- `splashes(dt: number): number`: How many drops hit the ground in `dt` seconds at this intensity (for splash particles, ripples).\n4590-- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n4591-\n4592-### type PrecipitationKind\n4593-\n4594-```ts","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0126VDctUAESqWUvrh2wWmDL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
