nes readable with a small light pool.\",\n    \"none\",\n    \"Expose analog gamepad triggers and more than one pad as first-class input, and ship a controller-first menu toolkit.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan carried working simulation code, regression numbers and a list of engine facts already proven. It saved hours and let me start from tested ground.\",\n    \"The size of the scope against one session, and a few plan numbers that did not agree with each other (a Saltline lap time, the placement of file names between the plan and the brief).\",\n    \"Breadth: 14 cars, 6 tracks, 12 tests, 8 events, a diorama of menus, attract, dev mode, split screen and hub play, all with sound written in code.\",\n    \"Mark a smaller first slice as the floor with the extras as a second pass, and include a rough career economy so the bot can be checked early.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Gran Tourniquet\",\n    \"tagline\": \"A slow and serious motoring life\",\n    \"description\": \"A calm pixel-art racing career on the Halcyon Peninsula: buy a tired hatchback, earn three licences, tune, and race for a prototype built in a shed.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Racing\",\n    \"source\": \"Gran Turismo 3: A-Spec\",\n    \"series\": \"Gran Turismo\",\n    \"players\": \"1\\u20134\",\n    \"controls\": \"Stick or WASD to steer, R2 or W to go, L2 or S to brake\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"pixel art\", \"vehicles\", \"retro\", \"third-person\", \"versus\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json'));console.log('json ok')\"; node tools/gen-about.mjs"}}}
