{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmEh6XHA6MXLwvMG12PD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both screens are fixed, and here is the bot run printed in full from the final build. The forced 508-check suite passed after the last code edit, and I rebuilt the HTML in `work/` right after it.\n\n**Fixes**\n- **Ending card:** the scrolling credits now stop above the Continue button. In the re-shot, \"YOU MAY KEEP DRIVING. MOST PEOPLE DO.\" sits clear of it.\n- **Pit stop clock:** a mid-lap start now shows a running race time. The pit-stop shot reads \"TIME 32.17\" with the crew around the car, instead of 0.00.\n\n**Whole-game bot, printed from the final build** (a script driving the real career code, no dev tools):\n- Series wins in the order the bot played them: dawn, fellow, feather, clay, touring, h200, gp. Feather took five tries because the bot upgrades only after losing a series.\n- It finished with 14,700 credits on day 73, with `kite, pico, moth, kiteCup, ryuRally, corsa, works, type9, ginga` in the garage, so the Type 9 is there.\n- The `play` suite passed all 26 of its checks, including winning the Rear-Drive Society after buying a Ginga.\n\n**Couch duel:** `tools/tests/browser.mjs` has the check, and it passes inside the 508. It starts a duel, confirms both engines are running, confirms the second engine runs the shared race, then disposes it and confirms the page returns to one engine. I did not re-show that check's own output separately.\n\nOn the monitor: its timer ran out, which is all the notification said. I checked afterwards that the review's own log showed all five scripts finishing with no errors."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":800550,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918},"output_tokens":555,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83ee8bb7-9f1f-4db7-994e-0a6a2ece78a9","uuid":"386445f6-1c7a-42f1-9277-790d8ac150bc","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:55:38.921Z","request_id":"req_011CgmEh66igUcWF71swQUsL"}
