{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmFWhHsaPxusjXApypap","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every listed 1080p screen has now been re-shot against the final HTML and viewed, with no page errors in any of the scripts. The HTML was not changed between the suite run and this pass; I rebuilt it right after the last forced 508-check suite and made no code edits since.\n\nWhat I viewed this time, all on that build, with the Pit-stop shot and the earlier ending-card check as noted below:\n- **Cars:** all 14. The six side-view shots (Longhorn, Heck, Kite, Libeccio, Moth, Type 9) and the eight rear views (Pico, Ginga, Ryu, Brandt 3.2, Kite Cup, Ryu Rally, Works GT, Corsa) show distinct silhouettes and tail shapes.\n- **Tracks:** the start line and a corner for each of Kestrel, Cedar, Harbour, Saltline, Red Clay and Proving Ground. Kestrel and Cedar corners are AI-driven on the road, and I viewed an extra Kestrel corner as well.\n- **Map:** day and night, with the night map's buildings and neon markers readable.\n- **Screens:** dealer, tuning, service, licence centre, event hall, settings and the pit-stop Handbook page.\n- **Race flow:** results, replay, couch duel, the Harbour night race, the Series Won podium and the ending card. The ending's last line, \"YOU MAY KEEP DRIVING. MOST PEOPLE DO.\", sits clear of the Continue button.\n\nI did not re-shoot the pit stop in this particular pass. I did view it after the clock fix: the previous pass showed it running at \"TIME 32.17\" with the crew around the car, and nothing about it has changed since.\n\n`exit-interview.json` and the single HTML are in `work/`. The Source Information and feedback sections are on the About screen and in my first full reply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10133,"cache_read_input_tokens":810807,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m